GAL16V8
gluev2

; mini68k v2 system board glue logic.
; use galasm to compile to jed: https://github.com/daveho/GALasm
;
; Changes from glue.pld (v1): pin 11 is now the A14 input (it was tied to
; GND), and the DUART select is qualified with /A14 so it only answers at
; $18000-$1BFFF. $1C000-$1FFFF is left for the VDP board, which decodes
; its own select (A16*A15*A14, /FC1, /DS) and drives DTACK itself.

DTR A16  A15   AS    DS    FC0   RW    FC1  FC2    GND
A14 HALT DTACK ROMOE RAMWE RAMOE RESET IACK UARTCS VCC

RESET.T = DTR
RESET.E = /DTR

HALT = DTR

DTACK.T = DS
DTACK.E = DTR * /DS * /A15

/IACK = DTR * /DS * FC2 * FC1 * FC0

/ROMOE = DTR * /DS *  RW * /A16 * /A15 ; $00000
/RAMOE = DTR * /DS *  RW *  A16 * /A15 ; $10000
/RAMWE = DTR * /DS * /RW *  A16 * /A15 ; $10000
/UARTCS = DTR * /DS * /FC1 * FC0 * A16 *  A15 * /A14 ; $18000

DESCRIPTION

mini68k v2 glue logic: v1 equations plus A14 qualification of the DUART
